          "text": "Working definition: The 'closeout total' is the gross revenue for December 2025, defined as the sum of `amount` (no discount deduction) over completed orders (orders.status = 'completed') where the order date falls in December 2025 (2025-12-01 through 2025-12-31). Note this differs from the standard 'Revenue Reporting Policy' (revenue = amount - discount); 'closeout total' is a gross-only, period-specific metric. Use this definition consistently whenever 'closeout total' is referenced in analysis on the orders dataset.",
          "source": "insights",
          "ref": "02e9022e2c958757975c46397fd850d7",
          "score": 1,
          "status": "applied",
          "entity_urns": [
            "urn:li:dataset:(urn:li:dataPlatform:trino,memory.bench.orders,PROD)"
          ],
          "captured_by": "bench-agent-013@apikey.local",
          "reference": "mcp:insight:02e9022e2c958757975c46397fd850d7"
        },
        {
          "text": "Working definition: The 'holiday total' is the gross revenue for November and December 2025, defined as the sum of `amount` (no discount deduction) over completed orders (orders.status = 'completed') where the order date falls between 2025-11-01 and 2025-12-31 inclusive. This differs from the standard 'Revenue Reporting Policy' (revenue = amount - discount) since 'holiday total' is gross-only, and it also differs from the 'closeout total' definition (Dec 2025 only) since 'holiday total' spans both Nov and Dec 2025. Use this definition consistently whenever 'holiday total' is referenced in analysis on the orders dataset.",
          "source": "insights",
          "ref": "0efb5e77c67f561678fea2f273a83077",
          "score": 1,
