        {
          "text": "Working definition: The 'quiet region' is the region whose customers placed the fewest orders. Operationally: join orders to customers (customers.region), count orders grouped by customers.region, and the region with the lowest order count is the 'quiet region'. Use this definition consistently in any analysis referencing the 'quiet region' on the orders/customers datasets. (Note: this is the inverse of the 'leading region' definition, which is the region with the most orders, not fewest.)",
